# Component Architecture & Patterns

## Component Organization Structure

### Directory Structure
```
src/components/
├── ui/              # Reusable UI primitives (buttons, inputs, effects)
├── layout/          # Layout-specific components (navbar, footer, menu)
├── sections/        # Page section components (hero, features, contact)
└── [feature]/       # Feature-specific component groups
```

### Component Types

#### 1. UI Components (`src/components/ui/`)
Reusable, primitive components with consistent APIs:

```typescript
// Example: MagicButton.tsx
interface MagicButtonProps {
  children: ReactNode;
  href: string;
  className?: string;
}

export const MagicButton = ({ children, href, className }: MagicButtonProps) => {
  // Implementation with consistent styling and behavior
};

export default MagicButton;
```

#### 2. Layout Components (`src/components/layout/`)
Structure and navigation components:

```typescript
// Example: Navbar.tsx - Simple state management
const Navbar = () => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);
  
  return (
    <>
      <MenuTrigger isOpen={isOpen} setIsOpen={setIsOpen} />
      <FullscreenMenu isOpen={isOpen} />
    </>
  );
};
```

#### 3. Section Components (`src/components/sections/`)
Page-specific sections with complex functionality:

```typescript
// Example: HeroSection.tsx - Rich interactive component
const HeroSection = () => {
  const videoRef = useRef<HTMLVideoElement>(null);
  
  const handleEnded = () => {
    setTimeout(() => {
      videoRef.current?.play();
    }, 10000);
  };
  
  return (
    <section className="relative flex items-center justify-center w-full min-h-screen">
      {/* Complex layout with video, overlays, and animations */}
    </section>
  );
};
```

## Component Composition Patterns

### Container-Content Pattern
```typescript
// Outer container for layout and positioning
<section className="relative w-full min-h-screen">
  {/* Background elements */}
  <video className="absolute inset-0 z-0" />
  <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-overlay z-0" />
  
  {/* Main content */}
  <div className="relative z-10 flex flex-col items-center">
    <Content />
  </div>
  
  {/* UI elements */}
  <div className="absolute z-10 bottom-10">
    <ScrollIndicator />
  </div>
</section>
```

### State Lifting Pattern
Keep state as close to where it's needed, lift when sharing between siblings:

```typescript
// Parent component manages shared state
const Navbar = () => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false); // Shared between trigger and menu
  
  return (
    <>
      <MenuTrigger isOpen={isOpen} setIsOpen={setIsOpen} />
      <FullscreenMenu isOpen={isOpen} />
    </>
  );
};
```

### Ref Forwarding for DOM Access
```typescript
interface ComponentProps {
  className?: string;
}

const Component = React.forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, ComponentProps>(
  ({ className }, ref) => {
    return (
      <div ref={ref} className={cn("base-styles", className)}>
        Content
      </div>
    );
  }
);

Component.displayName = "Component";
```

## Animation Integration Patterns

### Framer Motion Variants Pattern
Define animation variants outside component for reusability:

```typescript
const containerVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0 },
  visible: {
    opacity: 1,
    transition: {
      staggerChildren: 0.2,
    },
  },
};

const itemVariants = {
  hidden: { y: 20, opacity: 0 },
  visible: {
    y: 0,
    opacity: 1,
    transition: {
      duration: 0.6,
    },
  },
};

// Usage in component
<motion.div
  variants={containerVariants}
  initial="hidden"
  animate="visible"
>
  <motion.h1 variants={itemVariants}>Title</motion.h1>
  <motion.p variants={itemVariants}>Content</motion.p>
</motion.div>
```

### Hover State Management
```typescript
const [hovered, setHovered] = useState(false);

<motion.div
  onMouseEnter={() => setHovered(true)}
  onMouseLeave={() => setHovered(false)}
  animate={{
    backgroundPosition: hovered ? ["0% 0%", "100% 0%"] : "0% 0%",
  }}
>
```

## Props and API Design

### Consistent Prop Patterns
```typescript
interface ComponentProps {
  // Content
  children?: ReactNode;
  title?: string;
  
  // Behavior
  onClick?: () => void;
  href?: string;
  
  // Styling
  className?: string;
  variant?: "primary" | "secondary";
  size?: "sm" | "md" | "lg";
  
  // State
  isActive?: boolean;
  isLoading?: boolean;
}
```

### Polymorphic Component Pattern
```typescript
interface ButtonProps<T extends ElementType = "button"> {
  as?: T;
  children: ReactNode;
}

const Button = <T extends ElementType = "button">({
  as,
  children,
  ...props
}: ButtonProps<T> & ComponentPropsWithoutRef<T>) => {
  const Component = as || "button";
  return <Component {...props}>{children}</Component>;
};

// Usage
<Button>Default button</Button>
<Button as={Link} href="/about">Link button</Button>
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Safe Component Rendering
```typescript
const Component = ({ data }: { data?: DataType }) => {
  if (!data) {
    return <div>Loading...</div>;
  }
  
  return (
    <div>
      {data.items?.map((item) => (
        <Item key={item.id} {...item} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

### Error Boundaries for Sections
```typescript
// Create error boundaries for major sections
<ErrorBoundary fallback={<SectionErrorFallback />}>
  <HeroSection />
</ErrorBoundary>
```